{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 19: business accounts won by a sales team and lost to churn. The sales team doubles at month 12; new reps take time to become productive. }
Base Reps=
	10
	~	rep
	~	Sales reps before the expansion.
	|
Added Reps=
	10
	~	rep
	~	Reps added at the expansion.
	|
Expansion Month=
	12
	~	month
	~	When the new reps join.
	|
Sales Reps=
	Base Reps + STEP(Added Reps, Expansion Month)
	~	rep
	~	Reps on the payroll.
	|
Ramp Time=
	4
	~	month
	~	Average time for a new rep to reach full productivity.
	|
Effective Reps=
	SMOOTH(Sales Reps, Ramp Time)
	~	rep
	~	Reps at full productivity equivalent.
	|
Rep Productivity=
	3
	~	accounts/rep/month
	~	Accounts won per fully productive rep per month.
	|
Acquisitions=
	Effective Reps * Rep Productivity
	~	accounts/month
	~	Accounts won per month.
	|
Churn Fraction=
	0.05
	~	1/month
	~	Share of accounts lost per month.
	|
Churn=
	Accounts * Churn Fraction
	~	accounts/month
	~	Accounts lost per month.
	|
Accounts= INTEG(
	Acquisitions - Churn,
	Acquisitions / Churn Fraction)
	~	accounts
	~	Active business accounts; starts in balance.
	|
********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation Control Parameters
	|
FINAL TIME  = 48
	~	month
	~	The final time for the simulation.
	|
INITIAL TIME  = 0
	~	month
	~	The initial time for the simulation.
	|
SAVEPER  = 
        TIME STEP
	~	month [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored.
	|
TIME STEP  = 0.125
	~	month [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation.
	|
